EXT. SALT FLAT - DAY

A white plain to the horizon, cracked in hexagons, shimmering with mirage. In the middle stands a dead jeep, hood up, its shadow a small black pool.

BEATRIX "BEA" LONGSTREET, 40s, a geologist with a sunburnt nose and a scarf wound over her hair, stands on the jeep's bumper, scanning the horizon with binoculars.

MANUEL "MANNY" CRUZ, 30s, the driver, sits in the shade of the open door, a dry canteen upturned in his hand.

SIGRID OLSEN, 20s, a graduate student, lies on the flat, hat over her face. Her lips are cracked white.

DARIUS KHAN, 50s, a photographer, trudges back from the dune with a camera bag over each shoulder, as though weight alone could anchor him.

At the edge of the shade, PERPETUA "PERRY" NDLOVU, 70s, the guide, sits cross-legged on a folded blanket. She hums.

BEA
Nothing. Not a cloud, not a bird.

MANNY
Told you, Bea. Radiator's cooked.

DARIUS
Manny, you said it was fine.

MANNY
I said it was probably fine.

DARIUS
(muttering)
Probably.

Sigrid lifts the hat.

SIGRID
How long since the last water?

BEA
Two hours.

SIGRID
How long can we last?

PERRY
Three days, child. Maybe four if we stop quarrelling.

DARIUS
Perry, with respect, we've been out here since dawn.

PERRY
And we shall be here until someone comes. Sit, Darius. You waste your sweat.

MANNY
He wastes my patience.

DARIUS
I waste nothing!

BEA
Stop. Both of you.

SIGRID
I think I saw something.

Everyone turns. She points. A glint, east, wavering.

BEA
Where?

SIGRID
There, Bea! Past the dunes!

DARIUS
Mirage, Sigrid.

PERRY ^
Mirage, child.

MANNY
It moves.

BEA
It's moving toward us.

Beat. A faint DRONE. Not an engine. Wind in the flats.

SIGRID
It's a truck. It has to be a truck.

DARIUS
It's a mirage, Sigrid. It's heat on salt.

PERRY
Sigrid. Hand me the binoculars.

She does. Perry lifts them, calm. Everyone watches her face.

PERRY (CONT'D)
It is a man on a camel.

MANNY
A camel?

PERRY
He is very slow.

BEA
Perry, how long?

PERRY
Until he is here? Perhaps one hour. Perhaps never. The camel is thinking.

Laughter, cracked. Darius sits. Sigrid wipes her eyes. Manny drops the canteen and covers his face.

BEA
Okay. Okay. We wait.

MANNY
We wait.

DARIUS
We wait.

PERRY
(softly)
We wait.

The shape on the horizon grows. Slowly. A man. An animal. A long shadow across the white.
